      "text": "First, let's calculate the total number of outcomes the dice can show. Since each die has 12 sides and there are 5 dice, the total number of outcomes is $12^5$.\n\nNext, let's calculate the number of outcomes where exactly 2 of the dice show an even number. Since the dice are independent, we can multiply the number of ways for 2 of the dice to show an even number and the other 3 dice to show an odd number.\n\n- There are $\\binom{5}{2}$ ways to choose 2 of the 5 dice to show an even number.\n- Each even number on a die has 6 possibilities.\n- Each odd number on a die has 6 possibilities as well.\n\nTherefore, the number of valid outcomes is $\\binom{5}{2} \\cdot 6 \\cdot 6^3$.\n\nFinally, we divide the number of valid outcomes by the total number of outcomes to find the probability:\n\n$$\\boxed{\\frac{\\binom{5}{2} \\cdot 6 \\cdot 6^3}{12^5}}$$",
